# v2.15.10: three "docs" turned out to be raw claude jsonl transcript
# dumps — every line carried cwd, sessionId, agentId, model refs, tool
# payloads. Removed and pattern-blocked. If you generate a claude
# transcript into docs/ for research, keep it OUT of the repo — commit
# a rendered summary instead.
docs/taskgroup-user-manual.md
docs/dispatcher-tools-audit.md
docs/overnight-readiness-review.md
docs/**/*-user-manual.md
docs/**/*-audit.md
docs/**/*-review.md
docs/**/*-transcript.md

# v2.15.10: project rules for Claude Code sessions stay LOCAL, not in
# the public repo. .claude/CLAUDE.md historically contained references
# to private project names as "don't do this" examples — those references
# leaked simply by being in a public repo. Untracked so future edits
# never ship. New contributors won't get the Hive-specific dev rules;
# that's the accepted trade-off.
.claude/CLAUDE.md

# Test artifacts — never commit, regenerated on every test run
# (note: a handful of legacy files are still tracked from before this
# rule existed; the ignore here only stops NEW ones from accumulating.)
.claude/agents/hive-agent-*.md
test-multi-agent-report/screenshots/
test-results/
playwright-report/
/index.js
